# Maternify — Project Context

## What this product is
Multilingual communication tool for minority ethnic pregnant women in the UK.
Two flows: **Express** (symptom → English clinical script + TTS) and **Interpret** (NHS letter → plain-language explanation).
NOT a diagnostic tool. NOT a replacement for clinicians. Communication bridge only.

## Stack (locked — do not deviate)
- Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript (strict mode)
- **GLM-5.1** (Z.ai, OpenAI-compatible via the `openai` SDK) — primary generation
- **Gemini 2.5 Flash** — live fallback generation (`thinkingBudget: 0`, JSON mime)
- Gemini `gemini-embedding-001` for embeddings (build-time → `data/corpus/index.json`)
- In-memory vector store (no external vector DB; embeddings never in Supabase)
- Gemini TTS (`gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts`) for audio — PCM→WAV, base64 JSON
- Gemini multimodal for STT (voice) and vision OCR (letter photos)
- Supabase — text-only `corpus` backup + anonymous `events` (no auth, no PII)
- Zod for all schema validation (`safeParse`, never a second LLM call)
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Vercel for deploy

## File structure
```
/app
  /api
    /express/route.ts     ← Express flow endpoint
    /interpret/route.ts   ← Interpret flow endpoint
    /tts/route.ts         ← TTS audio endpoint (base64 WAV)
    /stt/route.ts         ← STT endpoint (Gemini multimodal)
    /ocr/route.ts         ← OCR endpoint (Gemini vision, image never logged)
    /health/route.ts      ← live/mock status
  /page.tsx               ← Single-page app (Express/Interpret tabs)
/lib
  /redFlags.ts            ← Hardcoded red-flag list (EN + Mandarin)
  /urgencyGate.ts         ← detectRedFlag() pure function
  /rag.ts                 ← retrieveContext() + in-memory store
  /schemas.ts             ← All Zod output schemas
  /prompts.ts             ← All system prompts (no inline prompts in routes)
  /glm.ts /gemini.ts      ← Typed clients with mock fallbacks
  /generate.ts            ← GLM → Gemini fallback JSON generation
  /rateLimit.ts           ← In-memory 10 req/min/IP
  /demoFixtures.ts        ← DEMO_SAFE_MODE fixture loaders
/components
  /ExpressFlow.tsx
  /InterpretFlow.tsx
  /EmergencyCard.tsx      ← Static, no LLM, full-screen
  /DeviceFrame.tsx        ← Phone-simulator shell (presentation only)
/data
  /corpus/index.json      ← Embedded NHS/Tommy's chunks (build-time indexer)
  /demo/                  ← Demo-safe fixtures + pre-recorded TTS clip
```

## Naming conventions
- Files: kebab-case
- Components: PascalCase
- Functions: camelCase
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE
- Zod schemas: PascalCase + `Schema` suffix (e.g. `ExpressOutputSchema`)
- API route files: always `route.ts` in App Router

## Hard constraints (non-negotiable)
1. All system prompts live in `/lib/prompts.ts` — never inline in route handlers
2. All LLM output passes through Zod schema before returning to client — no exceptions
3. `urgencyGate()` runs BEFORE any LLM call in the Express route — no exceptions
4. No `console.log(userInput)` anywhere — user input is never logged
5. API keys only in `.env.local` — never in source code
6. `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` is banned — React escaping only
7. User input passed as `role: 'user'` only — never interpolated into system prompt string

## Languages
- Input: Mandarin (Simplified) + English
- Output: Mandarin explanation + English script
- Red-flag detection runs on BOTH language inputs before any LLM call
